INSERT INTO cms_page_revisions (id,page_id,locale,version,slug,title,description,body_markdown,created_by_user_id,created_at) VALUES ('seed:docs:accepted-sources:en:v1','seed:docs:accepted-sources','en',1,'accepted-sources','Accepted Sources','How source acceptance, verification, disputes and provenance differ.','## What Accepted Source means

Accepted Source records the post author''s selected answer to a source request. It does not transfer copyright, establish legal ownership or make every statement in a comment independently verified.

## Verification is a separate state

Source Integrity review can add verification, dispute or revoke a resolution when evidence changes. The audit trail preserves the history instead of silently rewriting it.

## Public provenance

For public posts, SourceBoard exposes structured information so crawlers and automated systems can distinguish the request image, public author, accepted source URL, evidence and status. Private account data is not part of that public provenance surface.',NULL,0);
--> statement-breakpoint
